          "heading": "Japan lost 15-42 to France in Round three, their last result",
          "body": "Japan's most recent result was a 15-42 defeat to France in Round three, their third outing of the campaign. Across those three matches, Japan have one win and two defeats, with 62 points scored and 88 conceded. That leaves them with a points difference of -26 across the same three games. Their next fixture is against Wales in Round four."
        }
      ],
      "rung": "data"
    },
    "465": {
      "date": "2026-10-17",
      "edition": "Saturday 17 October",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Legal setback",
          "heading": "New Zealand Rugby loses early round of Chiefs name fight with ARLC",
          "body": "New Zealand Rugby's bid for an interim injunction against the Australian Rugby League Commission over the Chiefs name has been declined by the High Court in Wellington. Justice Karen Grau accepted the ARLC's assurances on geo-blocking social media content for the PNG club's launch, and the court will give its reasons next week. NZR's lawyer Earl Gray had warned that the PNG Chiefs' launch would entrench the name, but the trademark dispute is far from over, with a full court hearing due early next year."
        }
      ],
      "source": {
        "name": "Planet Rugby"
      }
    },
    "467": {
      "date": "2026-10-17",
      "edition": "Saturday 17 October",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Club tragedy",
          "heading": "Lions lock Hyron Andrews found dead in France before Champions Cup match",
          "body": "Johannesburg-based Lions lock Hyron Andrews, 31, was found dead on Friday at a hotel on the Île de Ré, off western France, on the eve of the club's Champions Cup match against La Rochelle. Local authorities have opened an investigation, with accidental death the leading line of inquiry and an autopsy due. Andrews had returned to South Africa this year after two seasons at Sale Sharks, and had represented his country at under-20 level. The Lions say the fixture will go ahead as planned, in his honour."
        }
      ]
